# The run-outcome divider's rule lands on the reference's row, and in the
# reference's grey.
#
# Both halves are needed and neither pays on its own -- the trap
# docs/visual-parity/REFERENCE.md names from both sides. Before this the rule
# was three rows high of where ref/02_thread.png draws it AND painted in
# theme::border() (62,62,72) against the reference's (48,48,62), and that band
# of the transcript cost 1,559 structural diff pixels. Moved and recoloured
# together it costs 64.
#
# The colour is Puffin's own: `AgentcloudTranscriptView.runSeparator` fills its
# rules with `Color(mutedText).opacity(0.25)`, which over the window ground
# resolves to about (53,53,65). The reference's rule peaks at (48,48,62) spread
# across three rows by the 2x downsample -- summed over the ground those three
# rows carry 30 units of ink and one crisp row at (53,53,65) carries 29, which
# is the same line.
#
# Only the POSITION is assertable here: the harness reads x/y/w/h/hidden/text
# and never a colour (afterhours_gaps.md #61), and the rule is drawn in
# on_draw_fg besides. The colour is held by the pixels in docs/visual-parity.
#
# The y is absolute and re-derived by rendering r9 at this window's own size
# and reading the element back, which is what the other coordinate tests in
# this suite tell the next person to do. It moves when anything above it in
# the transcript moves, and that is the point: the rhythm above it is what the
# reference is being compared against.
#
# settings: {"window_width":1180,"window_height":949,"open_tabs":["r9"],"active_tab":"r9","pinned_tabs":[],"theme":"dark"}

# Row top 289, 22 tall, so the rule is centred on y=300 in the element's own
# space and paints the frame's row 299 -- the reference's row.
assert_ui run_outcome_divider y=289 h=22
assert_ui_text "failed" hidden=false
